      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-29_WidnesExaminer_art0103" n="art0103">
        <head>WARRINGTON WAR 'INCIDENTS.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON WAR 'INCIDENTS.</p>
        <p>Bayonets Got Ready. A certain local firm have been engaged since the war sharpening bayonets. Their first order was in connection with the local Territorials.</p>
        <p>Saw Not .The .Enemy..</p>
        <p>Several ships from America and Eastern ports have passed up the Ship Canal this week. All reported that they saw liolo of the enemy's war ships during their voyages.</p>
        <p>-</p>
        <p>For Men Under Fifty, 4" „age The local Conservative Association i)'',-the to inaugurate a training corps, alld 811gt;i1, (I be age limit at 50 years- Such a WO used in time of need. •</p>
