        <p>'hi, Tug Boat Sunk in Canal. 411‘ steaming along the Manchester Ship tt'uring a fog early on Tuesday morning, r • g Walton, a vessel well known in the [i.ill district, collided with a large boat 17, and was sunk. Smitham, thz cap- l'ecia4 a very narrow escape, but an engineer Fl'e(l Crompton, of Parker-street, Din- e'ta! well as Joseph Owens (16), of Surrey- ' In the same town, was drowned.</p>
