        <p>Death of Mrs., E. Harmer. We regret to record the death of Mrs. Evelyn Harmer, wife of Mr. John Harmer, of Wilders- pool Brewery, which occurred at her residence, ,Wilderspool-causeway. Mrs. Harmer had suffered for a considerable period and the end came on Saturday evening last. She was in her 68th year. The funeral took place on Wednesday afternoon at St. Thomas' Church- yard, Stockton Heath, and many tokens of re- spect were shown by her neighbours, to whom she had become much endeared by reason of her help and many kindnesses to those around her. The Rev. E. W. Clarke conducted the service in the church and at the graveside. Floral tributes were sent by Mr. J. Harmer (husband), Mr. and Mrs. Beck, Mr. and Mrs. Broadhurst, Mr. and Mrs. S. Harmer and family, Mr. and Mrs. Jack Harmer and family, Mr. and Mrs. Tom 'Termer, Mr. Walter Har- mer, Dick and George Harmer, Mr. and Mrs. Emile Smith, Phcebe Beck, Mrs. Deck, Miss Lottie Hand, Edwin and George Deck, Miss 3.1 acloyde, Louie and Bert Holmes, Mr. and Mrs. Broady, Mrs. Grocot, Mrs. Cliffe, Mr. and Mrs. Croughton and family, Mrs. Smith, the Mothers' Meeting, Mr. and .Mrs. Hulmes, and "The Neighbours and Friends at Wilders- pool."—Messrs. J. Mounfield and Sons carried out the funeral arrangements.</p>
      </div>
