      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-08-29_WidnesExaminer_art0174" n="art0174">
        <head>DARESBCR</head>
        <p>DARESBCR</p>
        <p>Chorister Honoured.—Alr. C11314e6s Dareshury Church chorister'l 11 by the clergy and choir men3bel some eight-day clock, 'an the ec marriage. The pregentation the evening service on SundeS' who, after wishing- the recipient a, on behalf. of the choir, said 11e r 31l'..:t'sulke had i)eni a vela 11-oi choir froni criddhanit •:Cel'tlolsl ri rib, 10 speaker's) advent to the PA and conduct had been 111°6t ' thanking the Vicar, choirtutls,—rri; colleagues for so kindly renle111"-n-r Foulkes assured them that the K t always remind him of his please.llr. with the Daresbury Church Cll"is</p>
