        <head>SALES BY AUCTION</head>
        <p>SALES BY AUCTION</p>
        <p>;y Mr. FRANK HICKMAN.</p>
        <p>Situations Vacant.</p>
        <p>APPRENTICE Wanted to the Mantle and Costume Department.—Apply J. Atkinson and Son. Ltd., 18, Winwick-street, Warrington. laJ TINDP-</p>
        <p>_ —AESSES.— Wanted, two resident (sisters or friends preferred), for Ladies' Boarding School.—.-83, Bidston-road, Birkenhead.</p>
        <p>WANTED, by local tradesman, .-orthy Youth, about 19, as. Carter.—Write, giving references, Box No. T.S., " Examiner " Office, War- rington. WANTED, for Australia, twenty lads, 16-20, for farm work; wages 10s. to 15s. per week, all found; no previous experience necessary; parties sailing July and August, fare only £3, payable here, .£1 of which is returned by Government on arrival. Also ten experienced Farm Hands wanted, ages 18 to 45; wages £1 to 355. per week, all found; fare only £l, payable in England.—Write for par- ticulars to COLLINGS CO., LTD., Accredited Gov- ernment Agents, Rosemont-parade. North Finchlev. London: or 453. Strand. London. MAS Chocolate •Clubs.—Any boy, girl or adult can earn £1 to £lO spare time. No outlay.—Particulars Samuel Driver, Beeston-road, Leeds.</p>
        <p>Domestic Servants—Wanted. C66"' Cook-Generals, Parlourmaids, House- Parlourmaids, Housemaids, Free until Suited. —Miss Bowen, 16. South King-street, Manchester. COOK and Assistant Wanted; state experi- ence, reference and wages required.—Write Box 144," Examiner" Office, Warrington. COOK-GENERAL, superior; Catholic; not more than 30 years old; small wash; plain cook- ing; small family; another maid kept; personal references; X 18.—Glenavon, ,Crosby-road, Waterloo.</p>
